{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"papyral-scarlet-malamute","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Evidence-backed proposals to cut LLM token spend without weakening the gates. Full analysis in the session that filed this ticket; headline evidence:\n\nEVIDENCE (rebar tickets branch, Jun 23-Jul 29): 2,683 plan reviews / 779 tickets (mean 3.4, 71% re-runs, ~66k LLM calls, ~319 LLM-hours). Challenge repo (sec-semantic-layer, wk of 07-22): 545 reviews / 121 tickets, 70% needed 2+. Re-run causes (rebar store): 57% BLOCK->revise (intended), 22% staleness (13% self-edit-after-PASS, dep/base/registry drift), ~12% pure waste (117 unrevised-BLOCK retries, 114 identical-material re-runs incl. PASS<->BLOCK flapping on identical fingerprint+sha).\n\nAlready fixed upstream (do NOT redo): depends_on INDETERMINATE envelope bug (60a0eab88, 966f7cff3); container over-invalidation (f0cf30a0e); registry grandfathering (ADR 0053); trivial-rebase carry (ADR 0041); artifact dedupe (1bed2f0cd); temp-0 Pass-2 verifier (dcfcb15b4); prompt caching; budget cap+shedding; checkpointing; idempotent skip; --status; sign-review; claimability fast-fail; drift-refresh probe.\n\nPROPOSALS (no model changes):\n1. Fix the edit&&review-plan write race (EDIT commit lands after REVIEW_RESULT, voiding the fingerprint; only doc-warnings + resign rescue exist today). Sign on current-material==reviewed-material regardless of event order, or provide an atomic verb.\n2. Deterministic verdict reuse for identical fingerprint+sha when last verdict was BLOCK (idempotent skip covers only valid PASS). Kills unrevised-BLOCK retries and makes verdict flapping cost-free (~3k calls in-store).\n3. review-at-claim discipline: run review-plan only immediately before claim (a claim --review combined verb; next-batch aware). 245 self-edit-after-PASS re-runs + ~10.3k calls spent on never-landed tickets.\n4. Author-side deterministic preflight for the chronic blockers: P6 ac-quality failed in 456/540 challenge reviews; G6/G1G2/E4 + specification-by-example dominate BLOCKs. A zero-LLM lint (existing _lib_gates checks) surfaced pre-review would shorten the 57% BLOCK->revise loop.\n5. Close the Pass-1 usage-log gap (ed8c747e8 notes it) + real price table (COST_AGENT_USD=0.12 is a hard-coded guess) so the USD cap reflects reality.\n6. Demote AGENT-exec criteria to 1-TURN where the ADR-0054 corpus replay shows tool exploration never changed the finding: 18 AGENT criteria at ~20x 1-TURN cost dominate per-review spend (~26.5 calls/review).\n7. Optional, validate first: extend temperature-0 (or warm-then-fan-out caching) to Pass-1 finders; flapping on identical material observed (epic bbf1: PASS,PASS,PASS,BLOCK,PASS).\n\nExplicitly NOT proposed: model swaps (context-window/capability changes alter gate behavior; ladder + sonnet verifier already tuned).","id":"696a-82a4-47c5-4e54","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["token-optimization","gate-economics"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Token-usage reduction proposals for the LLM gates (evidence-backed, 2026-07-29 analysis)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785373897841792001,"uuid":"58acb854-4439-4d07-8f4e-9f0be54766ee"}